We add $\goldD{\dfrac{9}{16}}$ inside the parentheses, and subtract $\greenD{2}\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{9}{16}}$ outside them, to keep the expression equivalent.

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\greenD2\left(x^2+\dfrac32x\right)-2
\\\\
&=\greenD2\left(x^2+\dfrac32x+\goldD{\dfrac{9}{16}}\right)-2-\greenD2\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{9}{16}}
\\\\
&=2\left(x+\dfrac34\right)^2-2-\dfrac98
\\\\
&=2\left(x+\dfrac34\right)^2-\dfrac{25}{8}
\end{align}$
